# mutgap2_res_delete_object_11_bytes: DeleteObject (40) whose payload is 15 bytes: taskID, operation 1000, length 11, and three bytes of a buffer's reference. The FIFO passes the task the payload from the operation on, 11 bytes, and the resource manager refuses a deletion under 12 bytes, deleting nothing; the task reports success either way. The buffer was made by an exec, and its object-list entry was then rewritten to an invalid type, which a made object never re-reads: a copy out of it afterwards still completes with its bytes. A 12-byte deletion of an unused reference first leaves byte 15 of the FIFO's payload zero. In-process only (the service copies exactly the 11 bytes, and the reference's fourth byte would be whatever its heap holds).
